layout "layout.faqir"

block content
  p Every term used in this manual, in alphabetical order, with a link to where it is explained in full.
  dl
    dt#agent-key Agent key (agent token)
    dd
      | A key, starting with bba_, that lets a coordinator use the factory's MCP tools and nothing else. Created and
      | revoked in Settings → Factory.
      a(href="/docs/coordinator#token") More
    dt#allowed-roots Allowed roots
    dd
      | The folders a machine's runner may start jobs in, listed in its runner.json. Only that machine can change them.
      a(href="/docs/runner#config") More
    dt#backlog Backlog
    dd
      | The list of the factory's packages and their statuses.
      a(href="/docs/backlog") More
    dt#attention-bar Attention bar
    dd
      | The strip at the top of every page that says what needs you, such as "2 waiting for you".
      a(href="/docs/floor#attention-bar") More
    dt#bay Bay
    dd A machine on the Floor, drawn as a dashed box holding its stations.
    dt#belt Belt (conveyor belt)
    dd
      | The row of coloured blocks on a station: its last 20 tool calls.
      a(href="/docs/floor#bays-and-stations") More
    dt#coordinator Coordinator
    dd
      | The Claude Code session that runs the factory: it starts workers, runs the gates and integrates what passes.
      a(href="/docs/coordinator") More
    dt#claude-code Claude Code
    dd Anthropic's AI coding assistant that runs in your terminal (and in its desktop app). Buildyboy watches and helps steer it.
    dt#compaction Compaction
    dd When a conversation gets too long, Claude Code summarises it to free up context space. Shown as Compacting.
    dt#composer Composer
    dd
      | The page where you write and save prompts for unattended runs.
      a(href="/docs/composer") More
    dt#context Context
    dd How much of the model's working memory (its context window) the conversation fills, as a percentage.
    dt#decision Decision
    dd
      | A question from the coordinator that waits for your answer on the Decisions page.
      a(href="/docs/backlog#decisions") More
    dt#digest Digest
    dd
      | The daily notification that sums up the factory's last 24 hours.
      a(href="/docs/backlog#digest") More
    dt#done-when Done when
    dd
      | The list of checks in a harness prompt that tell Claude, and Buildyboy's Verify, when the work is finished.
      a(href="/docs/composer#fields") More
    dt#gate Gate (G1 to G5)
    dd
      | An automatic check a package must pass before it is integrated.
      a(href="/docs/backlog#gates") More
    dt#governor Governor
    dd
      | The rule that decides, from your subscription usage, whether the factory may start a new worker.
      a(href="/docs/coordinator#governor") More
    dt#herdr herdr (hc)
    dd
      | A tool that runs programs, including Claude Code, in terminals that stay alive and can be taken over.
      a(href="/docs/coordinator#herdr") More
    dt#harness Harness prompt
    dd
      | Buildyboy's built-in prompt template for long unattended runs: your Goal, Done when and Scope, plus fixed
      | guidance on working, testing, git and PROGRESS.md.
      a(href="/docs/composer#harness") More
    dt#hook Hook
    dd
      | A small program Claude Code runs at fixed moments (a tool is about to run, a turn ended…). The Buildyboy plugin's
      | hook reports these moments to the server.
      a(href="/docs/concepts#hooks") More
    dt#inbox Inbox
    dd
      | Where requests wait for your answer while walk mode is on.
      a(href="/docs/inbox") More
    dt#job Job
    dd
      | A Claude Code run started by Buildyboy on one of your machines, with a budget and optional limits.
      a(href="/docs/jobs") More
    dt#machine Machine
    dd A computer, or a WSL installation, paired with Buildyboy. Windows and WSL on the same PC are two machines.
    dt#mcp MCP
    dd Model Context Protocol: a way to give Claude extra tools from outside programs. MCP tool calls are pink on the belt.
    dt#package Package
    dd
      | The factory's unit of work: a module or a large slice, taken from start to finish by one worker.
      a(href="/docs/backlog") More
    dt#pairing Pairing, pairing code
    dd
      | Connecting a machine to Buildyboy with a one-time 8-character code that expires after 10 minutes.
      a(href="/docs/machines") More
    dt#permission-mode Permission mode
    dd What Claude may do without asking: default, acceptEdits, plan, auto, dontAsk or bypassPermissions.
    dt#plan-mode Plan mode
    dd A Claude Code mode in which Claude proposes a plan before changing anything. With walk mode on, the plan comes to your Inbox.
    dt#plugin Plugin
    dd The Buildyboy add-on installed into Claude Code on each paired machine. It provides the hooks and the /bb-… commands.
    dt#progress PROGRESS.md
    dd A file harness runs keep in the repository with what is done, decisions, failed attempts and next steps. Shown in the session's Progress panel.
    dt#project Project
    dd
      | A repository or folder on one machine, with all the sessions and jobs that ran in it.
      a(href="/docs/projects") More
    dt#pwa PWA
    dd A web app that can be installed on a phone's home screen. Buildyboy is one; on iPhone, installing it is needed for notifications.
    dt#redaction Redaction
    dd
      | Replacing secrets with [REDACTED] before anything is stored.
      a(href="/docs/settings#redaction") More
    dt#revoke Revoke
    dd Cutting a machine off for good. Its history stays.
    dt#rotate Rotate token
    dd Giving a machine a new key and making the old one stop working.
    dt#runner Runner
    dd
      | A background program on a machine that starts jobs for Buildyboy.
      a(href="/docs/runner") More
    dt#session Session
    dd One conversation with Claude Code, from starting claude to quitting it.
    dt#schedule Schedule
    dd
      | A job that runs again and again at times given by a cron expression.
      a(href="/docs/jobs#schedules") More
    dt#spec-ify Spec-ify
    dd
      | A Composer feature that turns a rough idea into Goal, Done when, Scope and a draft spec, by running a short job.
      a(href="/docs/composer#spec-ify") More
    dt#spool Spool
    dd The file on each machine (~/.buildyboy/spool.jsonl) where events wait when the server cannot be reached.
    dt#stale Stale
    dd A session that was working but has sent nothing for 10 minutes.
    dt#station Station
    dd A session's card on the Floor.
    dt#statusline Statusline bridge
    dd
      | An optional script that feeds context and usage-limit figures to Buildyboy.
      a(href="/docs/settings#statusline") More
    dt#subagent Subagent
    dd A helper agent Claude starts for part of a task. Shown as ✣ on the Floor and as its own lane in a session.
    dt#turn Turn
    dd One round of work: from your prompt until Claude stops and waits for the next one.
    dt#verify Verify
    dd
      | Re-running a job's Done when commands on its machine to check the agent's claims.
      a(href="/docs/jobs#verify") More
    dt#walk-mode Walk mode
    dd
      | The switch that sends permission prompts, questions, plans and finished turns to your phone and makes Claude
      | wait for your answer.
      a(href="/docs/walk-mode") More
    dt#watcher Watcher
    dd
      | A check Buildyboy runs every minute on each session: stale, loop, budget, context and harness alignment.
      a(href="/docs/settings#watchers") More
    dt#worktree Worktree
    dd A separate working copy of a git repository. Running a job in a new worktree keeps it away from your checked-out files.
